# STM32CubeIDE build output (regenerated on every build)
Debug/
Release/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# 4-mic capture outputs, loose legacy form (no --tag, overwritten each run)
capture.npy
capture_bearing.txt
mic0.wav
mic1.wav
mic2.wav
mic3.wav

# Legacy flat sweep outputs, superseded by captures/<session>/ below
angle*_capture.npy
angle*_trial*_capture.npy
angle*_trial*_mic*.wav
angle*_mic*.wav
validation_plot.png

# Session capture data. Audio is bulky and re-recordable, so the raw trials
# and the listening copies stay out of git, but notes.txt, quality_log.txt
# and README.md are tracked: they are the provenance of a session (room
# setup, wall distance, which trials were retaken and why) and cannot be
# regenerated from the board.
mic_sims_files/captures/**/trial*.npy
mic_sims_files/captures/**/rejected*.npy
mic_sims_files/captures/**/wav/
mic_sims_files/captures/**/*.wav

# Internal working notes, deliberately not published. CLAUDE.md holds the
# always-true hardware and config facts, HANDOFF.md the project history and
# open work. Both were removed from the remote on purpose; keeping them
# ignored means an absent-minded "git add ." cannot put them back.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md

# Internal tooling and working notes, deliberately not published. The hook
# in .claude/ guards the .ioc against accidental edits, CMSIS_DSP_SETUP.md
# records how CMSIS-DSP was vendored, and the supervisor update is a draft
# for one meeting. All are kept locally, none belong in the public repo.
.claude/
docs/CMSIS_DSP_SETUP.md
docs/supervisor-update-2026-07-22.md

# Presentation material: kept local while it is being reworked. The written
# writeup (docs/summer-writeup-2026.md) stays published; the deck, its
# figures, the generator and the slide outline do not. Delete these lines to
# publish them again.
docs/images/
docs/make_presentation.py
docs/presentation-outline.md

# Build and flash console transcripts, pasted in for one debugging session.
# Regenerated by the IDE and the programmer, never worth keeping.
newest build.txt
newest_flash.txt

# Bench and recording plumbing. Kept locally because it is how sessions get
# recorded, but off the public repo: the published tree is the simulation
# reference plus the analysis that produced the results, not the rig.
mic_sims_files/catch_audio.py
mic_sims_files/catch_audio4.py
mic_sims_files/run_session.py
mic_sims_files/replay_source.py
mic_sims_files/reject_trial.py
mic_sims_files/trial_quality.py
mic_sims_files/wav4_stream.py

# Superseded write-ups and working docs. docs/project-writeup-gdoc.md is the
# published writeup now; the handoff and bench notes live in HANDOFF.md.
docs/bench-checklist.md
docs/steps-forward.md
docs/summer-writeup-2026.md

# Superseded capture sessions. The published provenance is the deliverable
# sweep and the timing run; these earlier sittings stay on disk only.
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-22-inline-clap/
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-23-square-clap/
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-24-wall-65cm/
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-27-wall-2m/
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-29-angle315/
mic_sims_files/captures/2026-07-29-flash-check/

# PowerPoint lock files, and the stray root copy of the deck. The tracked
